{"name":"Shilo","hex":"#e6b2a6","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Shiloh (biblical city)","blocks":[{"text":"Shiloh was an ancient city and sanctuary in ancient Israel now located in the West Bank. According to the Hebrew Bible, Shiloh was one of the main centers of Israelite worship during the pre-monarchic period, before the First Temple in Jerusalem was built. According to the Hebrew Bible, after the Israelite conquest of Canaan, the Tabernacle was moved to Shiloh, and remained there during the period of the Hebrew Bible judges."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Ancient_Shiloh_IMG_2924.JPG/330px-Ancient_Shiloh_IMG_2924.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shiloh_(biblical_city)"},{"title":"Shiloh (biblical figure)","blocks":[{"text":"Shiloh is a figure mentioned in the book of Genesis 49:10 of the Hebrew Bible as part of the benediction given by Jacob to his son Judah. Jacob states that \"the sceptre will not depart from Judah... until Shiloh comes...\""}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shiloh_(biblical_figure)"},{"title":"Shilo (surname)","blocks":[{"text":"Shilo is a surname. Notable people with the surname include:"},{"items":["Andrey Shilo, Belarusian former footballer","Maksim Shilo, Belarusian footballer","Margalit Shilo, Israeli historian","Moshe Shilo (1920–1990), Israeli aquatic microbiologist","Ronen Shilo, Israeli entrepreneur and software engineer","Rostislav Shilo (1940–2016), Soviet and Russian director of the Novosibirsk Zoo and politician","Shmuel Shilo (1929–2011), Israeli actor, director and producer"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shilo_(surname)"},{"title":"Shilo (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Shilo\" is a song written and recorded by Neil Diamond. It was originally recorded in 1967 for Bang Records. Though not one of Diamond's biggest hits, \"Shilo\" has become one of his best-known songs, and was a staple of his concert appearances. It was included on Diamond's 1972 Hot August Night live album as well as almost all of his compilation albums."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fe/Shilo_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shilo_(song)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Shilo%2C_Palestine_%2813056127775%29.jpg/500px-Shilo%2C_Palestine_%2813056127775%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Shilo%2C_Palestine_%2813056127775%29.jpg/1280px-Shilo%2C_Palestine_%2813056127775%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Shilo%2C_Palestine_%2813056127775%29.jpg/500px-Shilo%2C_Palestine_%2813056127775%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Byzantine basilica, with excavations to the right.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShilo%2C_Palestine_(13056127775).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Tel_Shiloh_%28biblical_site%29_2017.jpg/500px-Tel_Shiloh_%28biblical_site%29_2017.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Tel_Shiloh_%28biblical_site%29_2017.jpg/1280px-Tel_Shiloh_%28biblical_site%29_2017.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Tel_Shiloh_%28biblical_site%29_2017.jpg/500px-Tel_Shiloh_%28biblical_site%29_2017.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tel Shiloh visible in the foreground","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATel_Shiloh_(biblical_site)_2017.jpg"},{"srcset